# Schoolgirl-alt — the same subject as schoolgirl.blob, authored WITH the
# instrument (blob:rings + blob:measure + test pins) instead of by eye.
# This is the treatment arm of a controlled experiment: schoolgirl.blob is the
# hand-authored CONTROL and must not be edited, deleted or copied from.
#
# Reference: docs/dev-notes/refs/schoolgirl-mesh/schoolgirl.glb (the SAME mesh
# the control was authored against). 115226 verts, standard 24-joint Meshy rig,
# bind T-pose, 1.700 m, feet at y=0, facing +z. 79% of its vertices reach a
# measurable bone — the highest of any reference in the repo.
#
# AUTHORED AT 1.58 m (= 0.9294 x the mesh), so every measured bone length below
# is the rig's own joint-to-joint distance x 0.9294. Measured off the rig bind
# pose (scripts dump of jointWorld, 2026-08-28; .l bones, .r within 3%):
#   pelvis (Hips->Spine02)        0.1037
#   spine1 (Spine02->Spine01)     0.1037
#   chest  (Spine01->Spine)       0.1037
#   spine2 (Spine->neck)          0.0544
#   neck   (neck->Head)           0.0790
#   clavicle (Shoulder->Arm)      0.1070
#   upperarm (Arm->ForeArm)       0.2291
#   forearm  (ForeArm->Hand)      0.2146
#   thigh   (UpLeg->Leg)          0.3686
#   shin    (Leg->Foot)           0.3504
#   foot    (Foot->ToeBase)       0.1270
# These are NOT corrected toward nicer proportions — blob:rings flags any drift
# over ~10% and the whole point of this file is to start from measured bones.
#
# THE RIG-vs-SURFACE OFFSET (same Meshy rig as bonewalker.glb, but this rig
# floats its chain HIGH): the surface crotch/skirt hem sits at 45.5% while the
# rig's Hips joint is at 58.3% — a 0.20 m gap (at this scale) with NO bone in
# the rig under it, and the thighs branch from UpLeg (52.5%), 9 cm BELOW Hips.
# The .blob grammar attaches every child at its parent's TAIL, so a single
# pelvis bone cannot anchor both the legs and the spine at their rig heights.
# Solve (the bonewalker's "deliberately long skull" move, applied once):
#   root pelvis 0.730 -> tail 0.834 = the rig's UpLeg height, so the measured
#     legs land the ankle at the rig's own 0.115 exactly;
#   bridge (UNMAPPED, len 0.191 = Spine02 - UpLeg): the rig's own root float,
#     carried honestly as a named bone no fit sees;
#   spine1..neck: every joint at its rig height (spine1 head 1.025 = Spine02,
#     neck tail 1.365 = Head);
#   clavicle parents to SPINE2 (tail 1.286 = the rig's neck joint, 1 cm below
#     the 1.296 shoulder surface line — the control could not do this split
#     because its torso was two long bones);
#   skull len 0.223: the face block rides skull at=0.45 -> cranium centre
#     1.465, midway between the measured chin (1.351) and crown (1.58).
#
# THE MESH IS DRESSED — cloth offsets are decisions, recorded here:
#   * SKIRT: A-line, stands far away from the legs (hem half-width 0.186 vs
#     thigh flesh radius 0.063): modelled as its own shell cone, never as leg
#     mass. Thigh sizing comes ONLY from the bare bands below the hem.
#   * BLOUSE: loose sailor top. Flesh taken 7 mm inside the blouse silhouette
#     at the ribs (blouse full width 0.254 at the bust -> flesh half
#     0.127-0.007 = 0.120), 4 mm at the fitted shoulder yoke.
#   * SOCK: thick slouched terry — the sock prim carries the FABRIC surface
#     directly (it IS the visible surface there); the shin flesh under it
#     stays at the bare-calf measurement (r 0.042) so the sock is +8 mm
#     fatter than the leg inside it. A rings suggestion that moves either prim
#     toward the other is the tool being cloth-blind (sock verts dominate the
#     shin bone's samples) and is overruled.
#
# MEASURED SURFACE LANDMARKS (this author's own mesh reads, 2026-08-28; joint
# -filtered + texture-classified per-vertex, so the T-pose arms pollute
# nothing; heights are fractions of 1.70 x 1.58, widths are FULL x/Z extents
# x 0.9294; per-leg numbers from segmented slices):
#   crown (hair)        1.000   hair dome to the very top
#   skull+hair widest  .94-.95  w 0.106  d 0.125
#   ears (pointed)     .86-.88  skin, stick out past the bob
#   chin / jaw          .855    w 0.045
#   neck narrowest      .84     w ~0.050
#   shoulder line       .80-.82 w 0.202 (torso only) — rig Shoulder 79.6%
#   bust (blouse)      .72      w 0.254  d 0.208  -> flesh half 0.120
#   blouse hem         .64-.66  w 0.199
#   midriff (SKIN)     .62-.66  w ~0.195 (bare, no cloth offset)
#   skirt waistband    .62-.63  w 0.219 (half 0.110)
#   skirt widest       .46-.48  w 0.383  d 0.294 (half 0.186 x 0.147)
#   skirt hem          .455     legs split; bare below
#   bare thigh         .37-.43  per-leg r 0.059 -> 0.063 upward, deeper than
#                                wide (r_z 0.066-0.069, deep 1.10)
#   knee (narrowest)   .27-.29  per-leg r 0.038-0.045, centre x 0.078
#   calf               .21-.25  per-leg r 0.042-0.046 (slim; no big bulge)
#   sock top (slouch)  .19-.20  per-sock r 0.050 — +8mm over the calf
#   sock column        .07-.19  per-sock r 0.045-0.047
#   ankle              .073     centre x 0.092 (legs slant slightly outward)
#   shoe body          .03-.06  centre x 0.092, r ~0.052, z-centre -0.04
#   sole                .00
#
# STANCE: the mesh's legs are NOT touching — segmented slices show knee
# centres at x +/-0.078 (1.58 m) with knee radii 0.040, an 8 cm air gap, and
# the columns slant slightly outward down to ankle centres 0.092 (toes-out).
# (The control authored knees touching — pair width right, split wrong; the
# front silhouette cannot tell the difference, the side view can.)
#
# STYLE: Ichiro Tanida early-2000s Japanese CG — smooth rounded forms, clean
# simple masses, toy-like. Paint palette measured off the mesh texture
# (per-class mean texels, sRGB): skin (216,175,138) mean / (236,211,186)
# bright-island, navy (2,4,106), blouse white (232,232,233), sock+sole grey
# (216,214,214), hair/shoe (25,17,9), NECKERCHIEF + nails RED (174,10,8) —
# the scarf is red, not navy like the control's.
model schoolgirl-alt
  # 0.9294 x the 1.70 m mesh — the control experiments at 1.70; sizes here are
  # mesh x 0.9294 throughout so the A/B compares method, not scale.
  height 1.58
  # Checked, not decorative — see blob-checks.ts.
  stance humanoid

skeleton
  # Root: children attach at a bone's TAIL (resolve.ts, no exceptions), so the
  # root sits at 0.730 = tail 0.834: the THIGH heads at the rig's UpLeg height
  # and the measured legs' ankle at the rig's 0.115 exactly.
  root pelvis at 0.730 len=0.1037
  # The rig's own root float (crotch -> Spine02), UNMAPPED on purpose — no fit
  # sees its length. Tail 1.025 = the rig's Spine02; every mapped bone below
  # then sits at its rig height.
  bone bridge parent=pelvis dir=up pitch=0 len=0.191

  # Measured spine chain — three short bones where the control has two long
  # ones. Slight backward lean: the rig's spine column rises z +0.034 -> +0.003
  # (at 1.58) over the torso, about -2 deg per bone.
  bone spine1 parent=bridge dir=up pitch=-2 len=0.1037
  bone chest  parent=spine1 dir=up pitch=-2 len=0.1037
  bone spine2 parent=chest  dir=up pitch=-1 len=0.0544
  bone neck   parent=spine2 dir=up pitch=0  len=0.0790
  # Carries the face block up to cranium centre 1.465 (chin 1.351, crown
  # 1.58); base 1.365 = the rig's Head joint. The visible neck is authored as
  # a prim on the neck bone below it (the house pattern).
  bone skull  parent=neck   dir=up pitch=3 len=0.223

  mirror
    # Clavicle on SPINE2 (tail 1.286 = the rig's neck joint, at the shoulder
    # line), side 0.030 = the rig's Shoulder joint x; measured 0.107 lands the
    # arm socket at the rig's own Arm joint (x 0.137 at this scale).
    bone clavicle parent=spine2  side=0.030 dir=side  len=0.1070
    # Arms rest DOWN and slightly OUT (the mesh T-poses; rings is per-bone so
    # this costs nothing). The out-angle is not stylistic: the measured waist
    # (0.098 half) sits exactly on the natural hang line of the forearm, and
    # at <=6 deg of tilt the two fields smin-fog together (solid -0.16..+0.16
    # at y 1.01 in the extent scan). 9/7 clears the waist by ~6 cm while the
    # forearms still swing FORWARD below the elbow (pitch 18) so the hands
    # rest against the skirt's front slope — the control's owner-tested route.
    bone upperarm parent=clavicle dir=down tilt=9 pitch=3  len=0.2291
    bone forearm  parent=upperarm dir=down tilt=7 pitch=18 len=0.2146
    bone hand     parent=forearm  dir=down tilt=0 pitch=12 len=0.090
    # Legs: measured lengths, slight OUTWARD slant (mesh centres: hip 0.062,
    # knee 0.078, ankle 0.092 — the toes-out stand).
    bone thigh    parent=pelvis dir=down tilt=2 side=0.062 len=0.3686
    bone shin     parent=thigh  dir=down tilt=3           len=0.3504
    # The foot bone only positions shoe prims (see the control's shoe note).
    bone foot     parent=shin   dir=fwd                   len=0.1270
  end

body
  # ============================================================
  # TORSO FLESH — a few large smooth masses; the garments are paint and
  # shells on top. Radii are the FLESH (blouse measured minus its cloth
  # offset, midriff bare as measured) — see the header for the offsets.
  # Blend 0.025 hides seams between overlapping bars without webbing the
  # neck-only band (the kk=4k reach lesson both this repo's torso rebuilds
  # paid for).
  # ============================================================
  # Hip/pelvis filler under the skirt (never seen; keeps the legs fused to
  # the torso). Half 0.095 x 0.075 — hip flesh, not the skirt's 0.186.
  blob torso on pelvis  at=0.45 r=0.095 deep=0.79 blend=0.020 color=ecd3ba
  # Waist: the bare midriff band (0.98-1.04) is SKIN — measured 0.195 full,
  # no cloth offset here. One tapered bar up the bridge (0.935-1.025),
  # 0.095 -> 0.090 half-width; the blouse hem is the paint boundary where the
  # bust bar's field crosses it (~1.05, mesh hem 1.02-1.05).
  # blend 0.008, not the torso's 0.025: alone on its bone it needs no seam
  # hiding, and 0.025's ~10 cm smin reach webbed it into the forearms.
  bar  torso on bridge  from=0.53 to=1.00 r=0.095 r2=0.090 deep=0.80 blend=0.008 color=ecd3ba
  # Ribs to bust: the BLOUSE is loose — flesh is the clean rib rows
  # (0.208-0.218 full at 0.66-0.68, the 0.72+ rows carried sleeve-cap verts)
  # minus its 7 mm cloth: x-half 0.106 at the fullest (1.13), z-half 0.090.
  bar  torso on spine1  from=0.50 to=1.00 r=0.085 r2=0.106 deep=0.85 blend=0.012 color=e8e8e9
  # Chest to the shoulder yoke: thin front-to-back (the blouse yoke is fitted;
  # shoulder band only 0.101 half and shallow), ends LOW with a tight blend so
  # nothing smin-bridges the neck-only band at 1.327 (w 0.050) shut.
  bar  torso on chest   from=0.30 to=0.85 r=0.108 r2=0.096 deep=0.55 blend=0.008 color=e8e8e9
  # The skin midriff SHOWS between skirt waistband (top 0.995) and blouse hem
  # (~1.03): the two bars above cross at ~1.01-1.03, and the paint boundary
  # between them is the hem line — a colour change on a smooth column.

  # ============================================================
  # SKIRT — one flared shell cone (cloth, not mass). Measured: waistband half
  # 0.110 at 0.995 -> hem half 0.186 at 0.719 (drop 0.276, flare +0.076);
  # 0.383 wide x 0.294 deep at the widest -> deep 0.78 of the x-radius.
  # Thin shell (abs(d)-0.006) clipped at the hem with a rounded rim so the
  # hem edge reads as folded cloth. tall 0.42 squashes the caps: the bottom
  # tall 0.06 (a flat cap at the waistband top) GPU-HOLED: render-check put a
  # 112 px hole at the waist — a 16x anisotropic shell (minScale 0.06) is out
  # of the renderer's family (the control's shells: tall 0.42-0.92). tall 0.40
  # then painted a dome of navy 3 cm ABOVE the waistband line (the extent pin
  # caught it: 0.232 at y 1.01 vs the mesh's bare-midriff 0.195). Final form:
  # tall 0.30 (3.3x anisotropy), base 0.112 at 0.975 — the cap dome tops at
  # 1.007, just 1 cm above the waistband, and reads 0.099 half at 0.99 where
  # the mesh says 0.110. blend 0.006: the shell is one prim — its only seam is
  # the waistband crossing, and 0.018's smin reach fogged the whole
  # waist-to-forearm slab.
  shell torso on bridge  at=0.738 r=0.112 r2=0.186 tip=(0,-0.256,0) wide=1.00 tall=0.30 deep=0.78 thick=0.006 clip=(0,-1,0) clipd=-0.719 rim=0.007 blend=0.006 color=01046a
  # PLEATS — the mesh's skirt is pleated (vertical shadow lines near the hem,
  # visible in the front render). Four shallow grooves riding the cone's
  # slope, cut into the surface: pleat LINES, not geometry.
  groove torso on bridge at=0.53 offset=(0.075,0,0.062) tip=(0.036,-0.170,0.030) r=0.012 depth=0.004 width=0.006 both
  groove torso on bridge at=0.53 offset=(0.075,0,-0.062) tip=(0.036,-0.170,-0.030) r=0.012 depth=0.004 width=0.006 both

  # ============================================================
  # SAILOR COLLAR — navy shell cape over the shoulders + back, front clipped
  # open (mesh: navy collar band 0.74-0.84 frac = y 1.17-1.33, w up to 0.45
  # across the shoulder pair). The rim is the folded edge over the shoulder.
  # ============================================================
  # tall 0.55 / at 0.80: the v1 cape (tall 0.90 at 0.86) rode up the neck
  # sides and read as a turtleneck; this one drapes 1.13-1.29 and opens the
  # front to z 0.06 so the blouse V shows.
  shell torso on chest at=0.80 offset=(0,0.028,-0.016) r=0.115 wide=1.05 tall=0.55 deep=1.05 thick=0.006 clip=(0,0,1) clipd=0.06 rim=0.005 blend=0.006 color=01046a
  # NECKERCHIEF — RED (measured ae0a08; the control's scarf is navy, the
  # mesh's is not). A knot at the throat proud of the bust plus two short
  # shell tails down the chest V.
  blob  torso on spine2 at=0.55 offset=(0,0,0.108) r=0.018 wide=1.25 tall=0.90 deep=0.60 blend=0.0040 color=ae0a08
  # tails run from the knot (z 0.108, proud of the bust's 0.085) down the
  # blouse surface to z 0.088 — the v1 lesson: a tail based inside the bust
  # z-half never shows. r 0.009 at x 0.030: the v2 tails (r 0.013 at 0.024)
  # overlapped into a solid red bib.
  shell torso on chest at=0.80 offset=(0.030,0.018,0.108) tip=(0.002,-0.070,-0.020) r=0.009 r2=0.005 wide=0.95 tall=0.55 deep=0.45 thick=0.005 clip=(0,0,1) clipd=0.12 rim=0.004 blend=0.005 both color=ae0a08

  # Neck: the visible neck (narrowest 1.327, w ~0.050) rides the neck bone
  # (1.286-1.365), x-half 0.028, z-half 0.036.
  bar head on neck from=0.05 to=0.95 r=0.028 deep=1.29 blend=0.0040 color=ecd3ba

  # ============================================================
  # HAIR — dark swept bob (measured hair/shoe (25,17,9)), bell-shaped:
  # widest just below the crown, cut to the ear line. Crown dome + side
  # lobes + fringe rim + nape, all smooth masses; front locks frame the
  # face past the ears. Plus the RED hair bow the mesh wears high on the
# right of the crown (red texels reach 0.94 of height).
  # ============================================================
  # Crown dome: centre 1.503, half (0.092, 0.085, 0.092) — hair peak to 1.58
  # (the smin with fringe/lobes shaves the march peak ~8 mm, measured).
  blob head on skull at=0.45 offset=(0,0.038,-0.018) r=0.092 wide=1.00 tall=0.92 deep=0.92 blend=0.0060 color=191109 gloss=0.22
  # Side lobes: the flare, outer edge ~0.098 at 1.46, bottom 1.40.
  blob head on skull at=0.45 offset=(0.070,-0.028,-0.028) r=0.032 wide=1.00 tall=1.30 deep=2.10 blend=0.0060 both color=191109 gloss=0.35
  # Fringe rim at the brow depth, hairline high at 1.45 (the decal paints the
  # part and the widow's peak — the mesh's forehead is open to 1.450).
  blob head on skull at=0.45 offset=(0,0.047,0.044) r=0.048 wide=1.30 tall=1.25 deep=0.95 blend=0.0035 color=191109 gloss=0.22
  # Nape: the bob's underside at the back, closing to the neck at 1.40.
  blob head on skull at=0.45 offset=(0,-0.070,-0.062) r=0.048 wide=0.80 tall=1.05 deep=1.00 blend=0.0050 color=191109 gloss=0.35
  # Front side locks: temple to jaw, framing the face.
  blob head on skull at=0.45 offset=(0.054,0.000,0.048) tip=(0.004,-0.118,0.004) r=0.014 r2=0.004 blend=0.0030 chamfer both color=191109 gloss=0.22
  # The red bow, high right of the crown, ON the dome (a small knot).
  blob head on skull at=0.45 offset=(0.048,0.078,0.006) r=0.017 wide=1.25 tall=0.80 deep=0.60 blend=0.0030 color=ae0a08

  # Chin: the mesh's chin is a definite point at (1.351, z ~0.088).
  blob head on skull at=0.45 offset=(0,-0.110,0.072) r=0.020 wide=1.20 tall=0.55 deep=0.90 blend=0.0040 color=ecd3ba

  # EARS — pointed, elf-ish, skin: they reach ~0.068 out at 1.34-1.38, past
  # the bob (the mesh renders them clearly).
  blob head on skull at=0.45 offset=(0.048,-0.088,-0.006) tip=(0.030,0.012,-0.010) r=0.015 r2=0.004 blend=0.0020 chamfer both color=ecd3ba

  # ============================================================
  # ARMS — white sleeve to mid-upper-arm (with a navy cuff stripe — the mesh
  # shows striped cuffs), skin below. Shoulder cap = the arm's core.
  # ============================================================
  blob arm on clavicle at=1.00 offset=(0,-0.016,0) r=0.030 tall=0.85 blend=0.0045 mirror core color=ececed
  # Sleeve: slightly puffed over the 0.024 arm inside.
  bar  arm on upperarm from=0.08 to=0.40 r=0.030 r2=0.027 blend=0.0050 mirror color=ececed
  # The navy cuff stripe (paint boundary = prim boundary).
  bar  arm on upperarm from=0.40 to=0.48 r=0.027 r2=0.026 blend=0.0030 mirror color=01046a
  bar  arm on upperarm from=0.48 to=0.98 r=0.024 r2=0.021 blend=0.0042 mirror color=ecd3ba
  blob arm on forearm  at=0.00 r=0.021 blend=0.0042 mirror color=ecd3ba
  bar  arm on forearm  from=0.05 to=0.95 r=0.020 r2=0.017 blend=0.0040 mirror color=ecd3ba
  # Hand: a slim smooth mitt, no fingers; the forearm pitch carries it in
  # front of the hem, offset z keeps it resting on the skirt front slope.
  blob arm on hand at=0.45 offset=(0,0,0.034) r=0.026 wide=0.85 tall=1.15 deep=1.25 blend=0.0040 mirror color=ecd3ba

  # ============================================================
  # LEGS — flesh at the BARE-band measurements only (thigh sized below the
  # hem, shin at the calf): the skirt and the sock are separate cloth prims.
  # Thigh cross-section is deeper than wide (deep 1.10, measured).
  # ============================================================
  blob leg on thigh at=0.00 r=0.062 deep=1.10 blend=0.0050 mirror core color=ecd3ba
  # Cone 0.070 -> 0.043: at the hem (t 0.31) that reads 0.062 — the bare band
  # measured 0.063 there — and swells to 0.068 under the skirt as measured.
  bar  leg on thigh from=0.02 to=1.00 r=0.070 r2=0.041 deep=1.10 blend=0.0046 mirror color=ecd3ba
  blob leg on shin  at=0.00 r=0.041 deep=1.05 blend=0.0048 mirror color=ecd3ba
  # Shin flesh: the calf is SLIM (per-leg 0.042-0.046, no big bulge).
  bar  leg on shin  from=0.00 to=0.44 r=0.043 r2=0.042 deep=1.05 blend=0.0044 mirror color=ecd3ba
  # THE SOCK carries the fabric: top 0.316 = shin t 0.426, +8 mm over the
  # calf, slouching thinnest at the ankle. Cuff bulge first (the slouch
  # bunches at the TOP: 0.050 at the cuff vs 0.042 calf).
  bar  leg on shin  from=0.42 to=0.97 r=0.050 r2=0.045 deep=0.95 blend=0.0050 mirror color=d8d6d6 gloss=0.10

  # ============================================================
  # SHOES — near-black (25,17,9) mary-janes, toes-out; sole grey d8d6d6 in
  # the mesh but no separate sole prim (the shoe body's tread reaches the
  # floor; the control's owner deleted its sole plate and the mesh read
  # doesn't need one). Authored as world displacements off the foot bone
  # (head = the ankle at 0.115).
  # ============================================================
  # Body: heel (0.092, 0.030, -0.075) to toe (0.105, 0.028, +0.055) — the
  # mesh's shoe mass sits BEHIND the ankle (z-centre -0.04..-0.066).
  blob leg on foot at=0.00 r=0.030 r2=0.026 wide=1.90 tall=1.05 deep=1.30 blend=0.0060 offset=(0.002,-0.085,-0.055) tip=(0.012,-0.002,0.100) mirror color=191109 gloss=0.20
  # Vamp/collar wrapping the ankle (mesh per-shoe half ~0.051 at the top).
  blob leg on foot at=0.00 r=0.042 wide=1.25 tall=0.95 deep=1.30 blend=0.0060 offset=(-0.004,-0.030,0.000) mirror color=191109 gloss=0.20

# ============================================================
# FACE BLOCK — the skin skull under the hair. Half-extents 0.066 x 0.076 x
# 0.083 (mesh head 0.106 wide under the 0.19 hair at 1.58), centre 1.464.
# The jaw carries the chin (measured chin w 0.045, bottom 1.351).
# ============================================================
face
  headRadius 0.072
  headWidth  0.95
  headHeight 1.30
  headDepth  1.16
  jawWidth   0.92
  jawHeight  0.80
  jawDrop    0.070
  jawJut     0.042
  # A small button nose — the Tanida profile has almost no nose mass.
  noseLength 0.002
  noseWidth  0.30
  noseDrop   0.026
  browHeavy  0.003
  browRise   0.024
  headBlend  0.0045

# The mesh's own face, baked flat and pasted on (see the skill: painted
# faces never read; three dispatches proved it).
sheet
  image       schoolgirl-alt-face.png
  decal       1
  # Aims MEASURED off the baked image (eyes uv 0.42, mouth uv 0.16, painted
  # hairline uv 0.70) and solved against the fattest head prim (crown dome,
  # centre 1.503, semi 0.092/0.085/0.085): eyes land 1.429, mouth 1.362 (the
  # mesh's own eye/mouth rows x 0.9294). The solved 0.71 was still a squint
  # in the frames; centreY 0.65 (BLOB_PROBE A/B, 0.60/0.65/0.71) places the
  # eyes at mid-face under the fringe — kept over the arithmetic, the render
  # wins.
  projScaleX  0.44
  projScaleY  0.33
  projCentreX 0.5
  projCentreY 0.65

# Skin: bright-island texels (236,211,186) sRGB -> linear (0.839,0.651,0.491);
# the per-class mean (216,175,138) includes baked shading. Toy-clean: no
# mottle to speak of, no surface noise, moderate gloss. Wounds stay red.
palette
  baseColor     0.839 0.651 0.491
  deepColor     0.50 0.08 0.08
  charColor     0.22 0.13 0.10
  specIntensity 0.45
  specRoughness 0.35
  fresnelBoost  0.30
  translucency  0.22
  surfaceNoiseAmp    0.0
  silhouetteNoiseAmp 0.0
  wetness       0.12
  mottleAmp     0.02
  mottleScale   1.2
  mottleColor   0.55 0.38 0.22
